{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE FIX IS UP — Gerrit change 1296, RED-first, squashed\n\nRevert 1292 is MERGED and verified against the tree: 'diff_inbound_parent' is ABSENT from\ngerrit/main's inbound_fields.py, so main carries no parent-clear path at all. The production bridge has\nbeen RE-ENABLED on that basis (it was disabled while the destructive code was on main).\n\nChange **1296** ('Clear a Jira-dropped parent only on peer evidence'), rebased onto current gerrit/main,\n9 files / +984 / -48. It re-applies the reverted scaffolding — the three-state parent read,\nfetcher.merge_parent_map, the nullable schema, the differ wiring — and adds the evidence gate whose\nabsence destroyed 63 parent edges:\n\n * binding_store.get_peer_parent / set_peer_parent: a new key on the binding entry beside the ADR-0026\n   baseline. In-memory until save(), persisted by the existing commit path, no new commit surface.\n   ABSENT is VALID and fails safe to NO CLEAR, so a v1 store, a pre-field binding, an unconfirmed\n   binding and an out-of-window key are all safe by construction.\n * reconcile._advance_peer_parent, called from _advance_baselines and gated on '\"parent\" in entry'.\n   THE LOAD-BEARING LINE: a fail-open read (get_parent_map degrading to {}, a truncated page walk) must\n   never overwrite a good observation with 'no parent', or the next pass reads a deletion and the\n   incident returns by a longer route.\n * diff_inbound_parent declines unless get_peer_parent is truthy. managed_refs REMAINS as a further\n   gate but no longer DECIDES — that is the entire lesson of this incident and of 2b16.\n\nROLLOUT BEHAVIOUR, stated so nobody is surprised: on the first pass after this lands, no binding has a\nrecorded observation, so NOTHING is cleared. Observations accumulate as passes run and the feature\nbecomes live per-binding. It self-heals into correctness rather than starting hot.\n\nEVIDENCE\n * the discriminating trio ('test_parent_clear_requires_peer_evidence.py') measured RED against BOTH\n   wrong states — defective tree fails the negative cell, reverted tree fails the positive cell — and\n   GREEN against the fix. Recorded in the preceding comment with the exact failure strings.\n * two cells in the original module PINNED THE BUG (they asserted a clear with no peer evidence). Their\n   intent is preserved and the fixture now states the precondition the assertion always silently\n   assumed; the reasoning is in the double's docstring, per this repo's rule for a test that encodes a\n   defect.\n * 2079 passed / 1 xfailed across tests/unit/rebar_reconciler + tests/integration/rebar_reconciler —\n   the FULL suites, not a targeted slice, because a green slice already cost this epic a CI cycle.\n * consumer sweep for the new binding-entry key: there is NO entry-key allowlist or schema in\n   binding_store, and 'baseline' and 'jira_id' were both added as new keys the same way, so no consumer\n   rejects an unknown key. Precedent followed, not invented.\n * lint (ruff + zizmor + actionlint), mypy (418 files) and the module-size gate all clean.\n\nMODULE SIZE: binding_store.py went 749 -> 795 and was tightened back to **787/800**. The operator\nflagged the headroom; extracting the last-synced-peer-state cluster is filed as\n[rebar:4522-e600-9e2c-4823] rather than bundled into a data-loss fix.\n\nSTILL OPEN ON THIS TICKET: 1296 needs LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, then submit. Its live cell\n('test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips') may still legitimately report SETUP FAILED — DC refuses to\nnull a sub-task's fields.parent (HTTP 400 'data was not an object') — which is the platform branch this\nticket's AC already anticipates, NOT the fix failing. Do not repair the cell."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785774611097553001,"uuid":"18c80b8e-da01-40f7-aecf-16a0e51e99df"}